<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anaukpetlun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1578–1628</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anaukpetlun was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/restored-toungoo-kingdom">Restored Toungoo dynasty</a> from 1605 to 1628. He reunited much of the former kingdom, taking Prome and Toungoo, capturing the Portuguese-held port of Syriam from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/filipe-de-brito-e-nicote">Filipe de Brito e Nicote</a> in 1613 and reconquering Lan Na in 1615. He was assassinated by his son in 1628.</p></div>
